<description>
Rotate each 2x2 block's four diagonal corner colors clockwise, then extend the rotated colors outward as diagonal rays.

Input structure
- The background is the dominant color.
- One foreground color forms one or more solid 2x2 blocks.
- Each block has four non-background, non-block corner pixels diagonally adjacent to it.

Rule
- Around every block, move the NW corner color to NE, NE to SE, SE to SW, and SW to NW.
- From each rotated corner, paint along the outward diagonal until the grid edge or another 2x2 block is reached.
- If a ray reaches a same-colored outgoing corner of another block that has its own visible continuation, stop the incoming ray at that junction.

Key insight
- The 2x2 blocks are color rotators and ray blockers; the corner pixels are not independent dots but the four ports of each block.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "colored corner pixels diagonally adjacent to each solid 2x2 block",
  "path": "after clockwise rotation around the block, each corner emits along its outward diagonal until the grid edge or another 2x2 block; stop at a same-colored outgoing corner that has its own visible continuation",
  "trajectory": "paint the retained diagonal segment with the rotated corner color",
  "transform": "the 2x2 blocks remain unchanged; old corner pixels are recolored by the same diagonal painting"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 8-12 rows x 8-12 cols, always square [observed]
  background: 0
  block_color: 2
  corner_colors: always exactly {3, 6, 7, 8} — one per corner of each block
  blocks:
    count: 1-3
    shape: solid 2x2 of block_color
    each block has 4 diagonal corner pixels (NW, NE, SW, SE) that are distinct non-bg non-block colors
    corners are a permutation of {3,6,7,8} — arrangement varies per block
    4x4 bounding boxes (block + corners) must not overlap between blocks
    each corner must be in bounds (block row >= 1 from top, etc., but corners on grid edge are allowed — margin 0 OK)
  input_content: only bg, block cells, and corner pixels; no other colored cells
  transform:
    rotate each block's 4 corner colors clockwise (NW<-SW, NE<-NW, SE<-NE, SW<-SE)
    from each rotated corner, paint outward along its diagonal until grid edge or another block's 2x2 body
    if a ray cell is 4-adjacent to another ray start of same color with path len > 1, truncate there
    blocks themselves are unchanged
  ray_lengths: 1-8 observed; at least some rays per example have length >= 2

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (input is simple enough)
  steps:
